.venv/
.env.token
# Any credential file, not just the one that happened to exist first.
# .env.setup-token sat untracked-but-not-ignored for weeks; a `git add -A`
# would have committed a live MCP bearer token.
.env.*-token
.env.token.*
*.token

# Raw benchmark output. Result manifests contain device tool output (configs,
# hashes, $9$ secrets) captured from lab devices; a raw vsrx-ci run was
# committed once already (da6a9b3). Keep new raw runs out of git. Publish a
# result only after redaction (MEC-192/193), via `git add -f` on the redacted
# file. Summaries (*.md) stay trackable.
results/*.json
results/**/*.json
